# What `mui init` writes as `build-sui.hxml`.
#
# It lives here rather than in `mui` because what a build for this backend needs
# -- which libraries, which generator macro, which output -- is ours to state,
# and `mui` had no way of keeping six of these honest. `$MAIN` is the only thing
# substituted.
-cp src
-lib mui
-lib sui
-lib kui
-D mui_backend=sui
--macro sui.macros.SwiftGenerator.register()
--macro mui.macros.Bind.all()
--macro sui.kui.Platform.registerWithKui()
# The markup needs two things, and a project made by `mui init` had neither:
# the backend's vocabulary, so `ui()` can check a tag against what this backend
# actually declares, and `mui_views`, so it builds this backend's own controls
# rather than a `nui.Node` somebody then has to read back. Without the first
# line a markup screen did not compile at all, naming neither -- which is a
# poor welcome for the way a UI is meant to be written here.
--macro sui.nui.Vocabulary.registerWithMui()
-D mui_views
--main $MAIN
-cpp build/cpp
